{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Gcx2zNp9RqVWbJcERJhoua","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I now have a complete, grounded design. Let me set up task tracking, then implement following TDD (Red tests first, then Green).\n\nKey design decisions settled:\n- **Turn derivation**: handler maps each `message_end` in source order; PI `turn_end` ignored; `agent_end` → accumulator emits exactly one LHC `turn_end`. LHC's own turn machine (`user_prompt`→open, `turn_end`→close, `turn_end` w/ no open turn→no-op) handles persistence + hard-kill tolerance.\n- **Abort disposition**: carried as a `runtime_note` (the only durable vehicle; research §5b: \"Mapper carries stopReason through\"). Update aborted corpus `expected` to match.\n- **Idempotency**: `eventKey` precedence entryId→toolCallId→responseId→content-fingerprint; handler synthesizes a per-session source index as `entryId` for replay-stable, collision-free keys; `turn_end` keyed by a turn counter.\n- **Failure isolation**: `invalid_event`→writable→converter records a gap `runtime_note`→`recordedGap:true`; `thread_not_found`/`storage_failure`→store unavailable→health signal, no gap. Boundary rule forces the converter to return a structured result; `index.ts` maps it into `SessionState.health`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3149,"cache_read_input_tokens":187715,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3149},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4562dd99-e915-4997-a6b6-c06f59211979","uuid":"65175e74-e3c5-4755-b8a0-925d9b80a244","request_id":"req_011Cc2k6DCavWCpfDKdZzhd6"}
